## --gc-sections, the default (ImplementationPlan.md 5.9.11, with the
## section 12 row 'Plan 5.9.11 amended (roots; M20.b)'): the units are
## methods, segments and commons. The roots are the entry symbol and
## '<msil>Main', -u symbols, NO_STRIP symbols (llvm.used), RETAIN segments,
## every INIT entry, every segment of a section that a referenced
## '__start_'/'__stop_' names (lld/ELF's -z nostart-stop-gc, so r2 stays
## although nothing reads it), and the table roots: every segment whose
## section cli::classifySection puts, under the triple's rules, in the
## constructor-table, destructor-table or unsupported class, which the
## writer runs or reports (TLS sections are not table roots). Besides:
## (a) a live segment in an explicit section (a SEGMENTS name other than
##     '.rodata', '.data', '.bss', '.tdata' and '.tbss') keeps alive every
##     segment of its object with the same name and the same COMDAT group,
##     or none, as lld/ELF keeps a whole input section;
## (b) on Windows triples every segment in an explicit section that belongs
##     to no COMDAT group is a root (lld-link /OPT:REF discards only COMDAT
##     sections).
## Marking follows token sites of live methods, relocations of live segments
## and symbols to their definitions. llvm.compiler.used retains nothing
## (5.8.10). Dead units are dropped, and --print-gc-sections prints
## 'removing unused section <file>:(<name>)' for each: a method by its
## function, a segment by its defining global and a common by its symbol
## (the section 12 row 'msil-ld texts and behaviour that 5.9.3, 5.9.11,
## 5.9.13 and 5.9.14 do not state'). Explicit --gc-sections is the default;
## --no-gc-sections keeps every unit. The cases:
## - g1.o: 5.9.11's roots, and the names of two dead methods and three dead
##   segments (unused_data, cu_data, and sc, alone in section 'other');
## - comm.o: an unreferenced common goes, a referenced one stays;
## - ex1.o and ex2.o, Linux, (a): dead_s shares section 'myset' and its
##   object with the live live_s and stays; ex2.o's dead_b has the same
##   section name in another object with no live member there and goes; in
##   section 'gset', gk_dead stays with the live gk of its COMDAT group,
##   while nogrp_gset (no group) goes; grp_myset, the member of an
##   unreferenced group in 'myset', goes with its group although live_s is
##   live;
## - w.ll on Windows, (b): the dead non-COMDAT wsec in 'mysec$m' stays; the
##   dead COMDAT member wc in the same section and the dead default-section
##   wdef go. On Linux all three go;
## - tab.o, Linux, the table roots: an unreferenced '.CRT$XCU' segment is
##   data under ELF rules and goes; an unreferenced '.tdata' segment goes
##   silently (--no-gc-sections keeps it, and it is 5.9.9's TLS error);
##   pre.o's '.preinit_array' slot, not in llvm.used, is a table root and
##   is reported as unsupported (the section 12 row 'Plan 5.9.9 and M20.a
##   (1) amended (`.preinit_array`)').

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj g1.ll -o g1.o

# DEFINE: %{crash} = --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

